  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Friday)\nIssued at 939 AM MST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nMean western NOAM ridging will support mild and dry weather as \nPac flow continues aloft. Weak/skirting impulses will support cool\nfronts at times to knock temps down a few degrees and support \npassing breezy days. Temps will be above normal in the period with\nthe warmest day being Sunday when highs will average 15-20 \ndegrees above normal. Upper impulse traversing the Northern \nPlains today, with warm westerly flow ahead of the system. Breezy\nNW winds will develop this afternoon across NW SD, with a few \ngusts over 30 mph. The next system is on its heels and will bring \nanother batch of warm air into the region tomorrow, with warmer \nconditions expected across the FA ahead of the system as highs \nreach in the 60s and 70s. Breezy south winds can also be expected,\nsupporting elevated fire weather conds across parts of the area. \nCool front will move through Sunday night. This will knock temps \nback down into the 50s and 60s for Monday. Zonal/mild Pac flow \nexpected through next week, with mild and dry weather continuing, \nas periodic cool fronts move through and support breezy winds at \ntimes.",
